// The production build. `tsconfig.json` is for typechecking and includes the
// tests; this one compiles only what the server actually runs.
//
// Splitting them fixes two things that shared config caused:
//
//   1. `dist/` contained compiled test files. They `import { describe } from
//      'vitest'`, and vitest is a devDependency — Render installs production
//      dependencies only, so those files could not have been loaded there. They
//      were never imported, so nothing broke, but shipping unloadable modules to
//      production is not something to leave in place once seen.
//
//   2. vitest discovered `dist/**/*.test.js` alongside the real `src` tests and
//      failed on them, reporting three failed files next to 52 passing tests.
//      That is fixed properly in vitest.config.ts too — a build artefact should
//      not be able to turn the suite red either way.
//
// Typechecking still covers the tests, because `npm run typecheck` keeps using
// tsconfig.json. Tests that are not typechecked stop catching the type errors
// they exist to catch.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "prisma/seed.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/__tests__/**"
  ]
}
